{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>שימה נא</b> — he returned to his place." "<b>ערבני</b> — pledge me, from «ערב את הנער» ( Genesis 43:9 )." "<b>מי הוא</b> — «with my friends» he will join hands."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {1 "The gloss is elliptical: Ibn Ezra cites Genesis 43:9, where Judah says עָרֹב אֶת־הַנַּעַר, to illustrate the binyan of ערבני.", 2 "Reading מחברי as 'from my companions' (i.e., among my friends); the syntax is compressed and the referent uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:53.987513059Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}